@page "/"
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveServer

<h1>Circuit pause</h1>

<p>
    This component runs in an interactive Server circuit. Two ways to pause it:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Server-initiated (Preview 4):</strong>
        <code>Circuit.RequestCircuitPauseAsync()</code> — open
        <code>http://localhost:5000/pause-all</code> in another tab while this
        page is open. The server asks the client to begin the graceful
        circuit-pause flow (used to drain circuits during deployments).
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Auto-pause (Preview 7, opt-in):</strong> hide this tab for
        &gt; 30 seconds (<code>AddAutoPause</code> with
        <code>HiddenDelay</code>). The circuit pauses itself and releases
        server resources until you come back.
    </li>
</ul>

<div class="card" style="max-width: 320px">
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="card-text">
            If the circuit is paused, clicking the button re-activates it
            (state is preserved).
        </p>
        <p>
            Count: <strong>@count</strong>
        </p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="() => count++">Increment</button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private int count;
}
